CVEstate
========

CVEstate builds on the CVE MCP Server (Apache-2.0, Copyright Mahipal
Jangra / mukul975) and extends it with the Watchtower estate-watch
system.

The foundation library — the 28 security-intelligence MCP tools, the
triage_cve orchestrator, the composite risk scorer, and the API
clients for NVD, EPSS, CISA KEV, OSV, and the other intelligence
sources — originates from the CVE MCP Server,
https://github.com/mukul975/cve-mcp-server, Copyright Mahipal Jangra,
licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. The full license text
is in the LICENSE file at the root of this distribution, and it
applies to the whole tree, including the new Watchtower package.

Watchtower — the persistent estate store, the SBOM and lockfile
parsers, the snapshot and diff engines, the delta brief, the four
Watchtower MCP tools (estate_add, estate_scan, watch_diff,
watch_brief), and the cve-watch CLI — is the new work shipped in
CVEstate 1.0.0, released under the same Apache License, Version 2.0.

CVEstate 1.0.0 also carries a packaging repair contributed by this
release: the mcp dependency is pinned to the 1.x line
(mcp[cli]>=1.7.0,<2.0.0), the fix the upstream project's own
dependabot branch proposed, so a fresh install starts the server
instead of crashing on import against mcp 2.x.

No copyright notices from the original work have been removed or
altered.
